MacBook T1 Support 0.6.0 beta

Ubuntu 26.04 LTS, amd64, generic 7.0.0 kernel and active T1 iBridge.

MacBookPro13,2 retains the full profile with Touch Bar, experimental sound
and board-specific Wi-Fi calibration. Hardware evidence is from v0.5.0.

MacBookPro13,3, MacBookPro14,2 and MacBookPro14,3 are hardware-unverified
Touch Bar preview models. Their profile excludes audio and Wi-Fi patches.
The camera shares the iBridge and should be tested after reboot.

Start with sudo mbp132-support preflight. Read the model and profile
before explicitly confirming sudo mbp132-support install. Reboot and
test physical operation. Use mbp132-support status for diagnostics.

To remove the driver setup, use sudo mbp132-support remove before
removing the Debian package. Preserve a working recovery boot option.

Full guide: https://github.com/joshuaypdx/macbook-t1-support
